Subject: [PATCH] ieee1905: mark raw control sockets with Linux network-control UP

The AL-SAP build sends over pnet, not EasyMesh's raw C++ socket. Set
SO_PRIORITY=256+7 before passing an owned AF_PACKET descriptor to pnet.
Linux maps this explicit priority to 802.11 user priority 7; existing
WMM queues can then protect control exchanges from bulk best effort.
Fail socket creation explicitly rather than silently send unprioritized
traffic. pnet owns the supplied descriptor, including its error paths.
The privileged unit test checks actual kernel priority and CLOEXEC.

